            <ArticleTitle>Two malignant peripheral nerve lesions of non-neurogenic origin.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>305-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/j.1754-9485.2012.02343.x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The imaging features and histology of two cases of non-neurogenic intraneural malignancy--an epithelioid sarcoma and myeloma--are described. These cases are important reminders that not all nerve tumours are of neural origin and also show the crucial importance of a robust multidisciplinary approach to achieve the correct diagnosis and management.</AbstractText>
